NOTICE:  scope copy public.facts_by_scope: no sift_col index on "public.facts", all 6 columns carried, table of 3.9 MB
DETAIL:  A copy carries the columns of the sift_col index of its table, or every column when there is none, and its indexes come on top of the table.
HINT:  Drop the copy and build it with columns => ARRAY[..] to carry the columns the reads need.
NOTICE:  scope copy public.facts_by_scope: run VACUUM public.facts_by_scope now
DETAIL:  VACUUM cannot run inside a function. A copy that is not vacuumed has an empty visibility map: a read checks every row it keeps in the heap.
